BT /F1 8.5 Tf 58 623.0 Td (Approval status: Sample only - not approved for use at a real facility) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 58 599.0 Td (1. Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 579.0 Td (This fictional policy sets expectations for reporting abnormal equipment conditions, communicating) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 566.0 Td (risk, and controlling follow-up work. It is provided as synthetic retrieval material for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 553.0 Td (industrial RAG demonstration.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 58 528.0 Td (2. Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 508.0 Td (The policy applies, within the fictional Northstar Process Works training scenario, to employees) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 495.0 Td (and contractors who observe or report abnormal process or mechanical conditions. It does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 482.0 Td (replace local law, emergency response plans, operating procedures, permit-to-work rules, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 469.0 Td (equipment-specific energy-control procedures.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 58 444.0 Td (3. Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 424.0 Td (Personnel shall promptly report abnormal noise, vibration, leakage, odor, smoke, unexpected) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 411.0 Td (temperature, alarms, or loss of expected equipment performance through the site reporting channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 398.0 Td (Reports should identify the asset tag and location, time observed, change or trend, relevant) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 385.0 Td (existing indications, and alarms or event references when known.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 367.0 Td (Personnel shall not diagnose a failure from a single symptom or take corrective action outside) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 354.0 Td (their training, role, and approved operating procedure. Do not approach a suspected release or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 341.0 Td (unsafe condition to collect additional information. Follow the site emergency response process and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 328.0 Td (notify the control room or designated supervisor when an immediate hazard may exist.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 310.0 Td (Inspection, adjustment, shutdown, isolation, repair, and return to service shall be performed only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 297.0 Td (by authorized personnel under current approved procedures and required permits. Equipment-specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 284.0 Td (isolation and verification shall use the approved energy-control documents; this policy does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 271.0 Td (define isolation points or steps.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 58 246.0 Td (4. Reporting and response) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 226.0 Td (The receiving operations representative records the report, acknowledges it to the reporter, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 213.0 Td (assesses it under the applicable operating and abnormal-situation procedures. Operations) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 200.0 Td (determines immediate operating actions within its authority and initiates escalation when) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 187.0 Td (conditions worsen, alarms activate, or risk is uncertain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 169.0 Td (The maintenance planner creates or updates the work request, verifies equipment identity against) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 156.0 Td (controlled records, assigns priority under the site prioritization process, and identifies missing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 143.0 Td (technical documents. Work shall remain on hold until required scope, risk review, permits,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 130.0 Td (isolation planning, and approvals are complete.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 112.0 Td (After work, the responsible supervisor records findings, work performed, parts, test results) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 99.0 Td (against approved criteria, unresolved defects, and the authorized return-to-service decision in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 58 86.0 Td (the maintenance management system.) Tj ET
